# Initial Setup's Servo Output page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigRadioOutput.cs.
#
# The claim: the page's constructor builds a row per output - sixteen, SERVO_32_ENABLE being 0 -
# each bound to SERVOn_FUNCTION, _REVERSED, _MIN, _TRIM and _MAX (ConfigRadioOutput.cs:11-69), the
# bars show SERVO_OUTPUT_RAW, and each control writes its own parameter when it is changed, as the
# Mavlink* controls do: the combo box and the check box at once (Controls/MavlinkComboBox.cs:
# 169-199, Controls/MavlinkCheckBox.cs:106-143), a number 300 ms after it changes
# (Controls/MavlinkNumericUpDown.cs:133-180). There is no save button. Each change is proved by
# the vehicle's echo, and put back.
#
# Output 9 is used because a quad leaves it Disabled; nothing is connected to it in SITL.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, whose
# outputs are the firmware's defaults: 1-4 Motor1-Motor4, the rest Disabled, every one 1100 /
# 1500 / 1900 and not reversed. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-servo.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way can leave SERVO9_TRIM at 1510, SERVO9_REVERSED at 1 or
# SERVO9_FUNCTION at 1; the first expectations below then fail until a fresh SITL.

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6

# Initial Setup lists the page once every parameter is in (isConnected && gotAllParams,
# InitialSetup.cs:213-216), and here parameters are downloaded when asked for.
click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.SERVO9_TRIM 1500
expect params.value.SERVO9_FUNCTION 0
expect params.value.SERVO9_REVERSED 0

click tab-setup
expect config.servo.active false
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigRadioOutput
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigRadioOutput
expect config.servo.active true
expect config.servo.rows 16

# What the constructor read.
expect config.servo.1.function 33
expect config.servo.1.function.text Motor1
expect config.servo.1.function.enabled true
expect config.servo.4.function.text Motor4
expect config.servo.9.function 0
expect config.servo.9.function.text Disabled
expect config.servo.1.reversed unchecked
expect config.servo.1.min 1100
expect config.servo.1.trim 1500
expect config.servo.1.max 1900
expect config.servo.16.max 1900
# The bars are SERVO_OUTPUT_RAW: a disarmed copter holds its motors at the bottom of their range.
expect config.servo.1.position >= 900
expect config.servo.write none

# A typed trim, read on Enter and written 300 ms later.
click servo-SERVO9_TRIM
expect config.servo.editing SERVO9_TRIM
key ctrl+u
type 1510
key Return
settle 2
expect config.servo.9.trim 1510
expect config.servo.write SERVO9_TRIM 1510 accepted
expect params.value.SERVO9_TRIM 1510

# The arrows step by one: down to 1509, and the timer writes it.
click servo-SERVO9_TRIM-down
settle 2
expect config.servo.9.trim 1509
expect config.servo.write SERVO9_TRIM 1509 accepted
expect params.value.SERVO9_TRIM 1509

# And back to 1500.
click servo-SERVO9_TRIM
key ctrl+u
type 1500
key Return
settle 2
expect config.servo.write SERVO9_TRIM 1500 accepted
expect params.value.SERVO9_TRIM 1500

# The Reverse box writes 1, then 0.
click servo-SERVO9_REVERSED
settle 2
expect config.servo.9.reversed checked
expect config.servo.write SERVO9_REVERSED 1 accepted
expect params.value.SERVO9_REVERSED 1
click servo-SERVO9_REVERSED
settle 2
expect config.servo.9.reversed unchecked
expect params.value.SERVO9_REVERSED 0

# The function: RCPassThru, then Disabled again. The list shows thirty rows and scrolls three a
# wheel notch, as Mission Planner's drop-down scrolls; RCPassThru is row 96 of the fetched
# documentation's list, which orders a SERVOn_FUNCTION's 128 values alphabetically after GPIO and
# Disabled. Forty notches down stops at the end (row 98 on top), two up puts 92 on top and row 96
# in view.
click servo-SERVO9_FUNCTION
expect config.servo.list.top 0
scroll servo-SERVO9_FUNCTION-list down 40
expect config.servo.list.top 98
scroll servo-SERVO9_FUNCTION-list up 2
expect config.servo.list.top 92
click servo-SERVO9_FUNCTION-1
settle 2
expect config.servo.9.function 1
expect config.servo.9.function.text RCPassThru
expect config.servo.write SERVO9_FUNCTION 1 accepted
expect params.value.SERVO9_FUNCTION 1
# Opened on the selected row - RCPassThru at the bottom of the thirty - so Disabled, row 1, is
# out of view until the wheel brings the top back.
click servo-SERVO9_FUNCTION
expect config.servo.list.top 67
scroll servo-SERVO9_FUNCTION-list up 40
expect config.servo.list.top 0
click servo-SERVO9_FUNCTION-0
settle 2
expect config.servo.9.function 0
expect params.value.SERVO9_FUNCTION 0
expect config.servo.message none
expect config.servo.writes.pending 0

# Choosing another page deactivates this one (BackstageView.cs:453-464).
click setup-page-ConfigFlightModes
expect setup.page ConfigFlightModes
expect config.servo.active false
